    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="0703" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/295</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-08">April 8, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called to see me this morning. The Ambassador stated that
                    he had just received a cable from his Foreign Office stating that the British
                    Government agreed to the proposals of <pb facs="0704" n="692" xml:id="pg692"/>
                    this Government concerning the manner of determining the Lease-Lend material to
                    be furnished Turkey.</p>
                <p>I said that I was very glad to receive this information and that I trusted that
                    his Embassy would immediately discuss these questions with Mr. Acheson.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
